{
  "description": "Cases for the prototype mark data-doan-prototype=\"<width>x<height>\". Read by Go (canvas parser, doan check) and by TypeScript (renderer judgment, the prototype window's injected script). values: each raw attribute value with whether it is valid under ^[1-9][0-9]{0,4}x[1-9][0-9]{0,4}$ (anchored to the whole string, no trimming, no multiline) and, when valid, its parsed width and height. placements: a body fragment with the marks a parser must report outside <template>: frames lists every data-doan-frame element in document order with its raw mark (null when absent); stray lists the raw marks on elements without data-doan-frame, in document order; codes lists the doan check codes about marks the fragment must produce (invalid_prototype_size for an invalid mark on a frame, prototype_not_frame for any mark on a non-frame element; a non-frame mark is never also judged for its size). Frames and marks inside <template> do not count.",
